---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-16">
    {/* Back Arrow */}
    <div class="mb-8">
      <a href="/" class="inline-flex items-center text-primary hover:text-white transition-colors">
        <svg class="w-6 h-6 mr-2" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7" />
        </svg>
        Back to Home
      </a>
    </div>

    <header class="mb-12 text-center">
      <h1 class="mb-6 font-serif text-4xl font-bold text-white">
        LED-Based Countdown Timer
      </h1>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none">
      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="mb-4 font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-primary">Project Overview</h2>
        <p class="text-neutral">Together with my teammate, I designed and built a four-digit countdown timer for our Circuits and Electronics course. The project used custom 7-segment LED displays (each segment assembled from discrete LEDs), controlled by an Arduino Uno, with a potentiometer for time adjustment and a buzzer for alerts.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="mb-4 font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-primary">Key Features</h2>
        <ul class="text-neutral list-disc list-inside space-y-2">
          <li>Custom four-digit display built from individual LEDs</li>
          <li>Arduino Uno for countdown logic and display multiplexing</li>
          <li>Buzzer alarms at halfway, one-minute remaining, and countdown completion</li>
          <li>Potentiometer input for precise time setting</li>
          <li>Custom circuit with transistors and capacitors for efficient multiplexing and signal smoothing</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="mb-4 font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-primary">Technical Implementation</h2>
        <ul class="text-neutral list-disc list-inside space-y-2">
          <li>Multiplexing with NPN transistors to drive four LED digits and a colon indicator</li>
          <li>Resistor-based current regulation for LED brightness and safety (470 Ω per segment, 1 kΩ at transistor bases)</li>
          <li>Analog input processing from a 10 kΩ potentiometer for user-controlled time settings</li>
          <li>PWM control for buzzer signaling</li>
          <li>Power regulation with a transformer, LM7805 voltage regulator, and smoothing capacitors (100 µF, 470 µF)</li>
          <li>Arduino C++ programming for countdown logic, LED digit rendering, and alert management</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="mb-4 font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-primary">Challenges & Improvements</h2>
        <ul class="text-neutral list-disc list-inside space-y-2">
          <li>Breadboard wiring complexity: multiplexing required careful layout to avoid messy bundling.</li>
          <li>LED availability: limited red and green LEDs led us to substitute with yellow.</li>
          <li>Flickering issues: mitigated by increasing capacitor sizes for better voltage stability.</li>
          <li>Future improvements include designing a custom PCB for portability, better aesthetics, and reduced wiring complexity.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="mb-6 font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-primary">Media</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
          <div class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-lg cursor-pointer" onclick="openImageModal('/thadeandme.png', 'LED-Based Countdown Timer')">
            <img src="/thadeandme.png" alt="LED-Based Countdown Timer" class="w-full h-auto object-cover transition-transform duration-300 hover:scale-105" />
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="flex justify-center">
        <a href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1RK3p15yb5aZGQdGx3MCCLqXXD7TcWJDG/view?usp=sharing" target="_blank" class="rounded-full bg-primary px-8 py-4 text-white font-medium hover:bg-primary/90 transition-colors after:ml-2 after:content-[url(/external.svg)]">
          View Demo Video
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <!-- Image Modal -->
  <div id="imageModal" class="fixed inset-0 bg-black bg-opacity-90 z-50 hidden flex items-center justify-center p-4">
    <div class="relative max-w-4xl max-h-full">
      <button 
        id="closeModal" 
        class="absolute top-4 right-4 text-white hover:text-gray-300 transition-colors z-10 bg-black bg-opacity-50 rounded-full p-2"
        onclick="closeImageModal()"
      >
        <svg class="w-8 h-8" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M6 18L18 6M6 6l12 12" />
        </svg>
      </button>
      <img id="modalImage" src="" alt="" class="max-w-full max-h-full object-contain rounded-lg" />
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<script>
  function openImageModal(src: string, alt: string) {
    const modal = document.getElementById('imageModal');
    const modalImage = document.getElementById('modalImage') as HTMLImageElement;
    
    if (!modal || !modalImage) return;
    
    modalImage.src = src;
    modalImage.alt = alt;
    modal.classList.remove('hidden');
    document.body.style.overflow = 'hidden';
  }

  function closeImageModal() {
    const modal = document.getElementById('imageModal');
    if (!modal) return;
    
    modal.classList.add('hidden');
    document.body.style.overflow = 'auto';
  }

  // Close modal when clicking outside the image
  document.addEventListener('click', (e: Event) => {
    const modal = document.getElementById('imageModal');
    const modalElement = e.target as HTMLElement;
    
    if (modal && modalElement && modalElement.id === 'imageModal') {
      closeImageModal();
    }
  });

  // Close modal with Escape key
  document.addEventListener('keydown', (e: KeyboardEvent) => {
    if (e.key === 'Escape') {
      closeImageModal();
    }
  });
</script>